Sparky Stereo OS (ORDER 50 step 5): ParaView offers one stereo output, the declared pair (patch 0001). The render views start as a stereo pair handed to the desktop (Crystal Eyes, which the edition's Mesa packs side by side and declares to Stereo KWin), and the desktop makes each screen's format. "Enable 3D", a Render View setting on by default, decides it at ParaView's start; the View menu gains "Enable 3D" and "3D display settings..." (KScreen).
ParaView's own stereo output formats (Red-Blue, Interlaced, Dresden, Anaglyph, Checkerboard, SplitViewportHorizontal) are not offered: --stereo-type takes 'Crystal Eyes' only and refuses the others with what to use instead, the Render View's stereo types are not shown in the properties panel, the screenshot's stereo modes keep No change, No stereo, Left Eye Only, Right Eye Only and Both Eyes. A state file or a saved setting that names one of the six opens in the pair and the person is told once; a view the desktop shows flat is said once. Every input and every other function stays.
On Wayland, ParaView's caution "not fully tested on Wayland" is logged at INFO and no longer opens the Output Messages window at every start (patch 0002): Wayland is the route the edition tests and ships.
The sentences are in the gettext domain paraview-stereo (translations/paraview-stereo.po.patch: pt_BR, and the edition's two labels in the eight other languages); Build-Depends gains gettext.
The source and the architecture-dependent packages are built (--build=source,any); paraview-doc stays Debian's. The debug information is kept, compressed in the objects and the linked files.
Maintainer: Daniel Ramos (Capitain Jack); Original-Maintainer: Debian Science Maintainers; Homepage and Bugs: the edition's.
Sparky Stereo OS (ORDER 50 step 5): with Enable 3D off ParaView starts flat (it crashed at every start: the mono widget was asked for a stereo format); the told-once notices open after the view has drawn and open again when Qt replaces the main window's platform window under them (on Wayland that closed them, on xcb it hid them), and their sentences also go to the log; a state file naming a former output format is told too (it opened in the pair without a word) (patch 0003).
